{"kind":"report","text":"Adopted as proposed, together with 9455d1c5. For opt-in scopes only: before any directly signed genesis is recorded, the matching string body must be present for every typed detached-text digest that its genesis input names. A missing or non-matching body is answered bad-field, and no genesis is written. So every recorded opt-in birth has a derivable set of retained child declarations and bodies, and replay counts that set at genesis. Older scopes keep their current behaviour, including recorded refused geneses, and no recorded Input or diagnosis format changes. Child deliveries already fetch named bodies before the turn, so they need no change. Your conservative handling of older scopes stands: where presence at birth cannot be proved, report the bytes as incomplete. A later alias never counts as proof that a body was present at birth.","body":{"decision":"adopt: opt-in genesis requires every named detached-text body; otherwise bad-field, no genesis","request":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2c76d80c3c4575688b9485c1bf442ebbcec29db0","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}